&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;SOFTWARE.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="what-this-means"&gt;What This Means&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are free to:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Quick Start</title><link>/docs/getting-started/quick-start/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/getting-started/quick-start/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Get typing in under a minute with this quick start guide!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="terminal-mode"&gt;Terminal Mode&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The simplest way to start:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;baboon
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;That&amp;rsquo;s it! You&amp;rsquo;ll see a word displayed in large block letters. Start typing!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="what-youll-see"&gt;What You&amp;rsquo;ll See&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Word&lt;/strong&gt; - Displayed in large block letters in the center&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Progress&lt;/strong&gt; - Shows &amp;ldquo;Word X/30&amp;rdquo; in the header&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WPM Bar&lt;/strong&gt; - Live words-per-minute displayed at the bottom&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h3 id="how-to-play"&gt;How to Play&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Type the letters you see&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Letters turn &lt;strong&gt;green&lt;/strong&gt; when correct, &lt;strong&gt;red&lt;/strong&gt; when wrong&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Press &lt;span class="keyboard-key "&gt;Space&lt;/span&gt;
 when you&amp;rsquo;ve typed the whole word&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete 30 words to finish the round&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;View your statistics on the results screen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h3 id="keyboard-shortcuts"&gt;Keyboard Shortcuts&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
 &lt;thead&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;Key&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;Action&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/thead&gt;
 &lt;tbody&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;span class="keyboard-key "&gt;Space&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Advance to next word&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;span class="keyboard-key "&gt;Backspace&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Delete last character&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;span class="keyboard-key "&gt;Ctrl+W&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Clear entire word&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;span class="keyboard-key "&gt;Tab&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Restart round&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;span class="keyboard-key "&gt;Ctrl+O&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Open options&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;span class="keyboard-key "&gt;Esc&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Exit&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2 id="web-mode"&gt;Web Mode&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For a beautiful browser-based experience:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Structs</title><link>/docs/go-tutorial/02-settings/structs/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/go-tutorial/02-settings/structs/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="structs"&gt;Structs&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Structs are Go&amp;rsquo;s way of grouping related data together. They&amp;rsquo;re similar to classes in other languages, but simpler - they&amp;rsquo;re just data containers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="defining-a-struct"&gt;Defining a Struct&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s how Baboon defines the &lt;code&gt;Settings&lt;/code&gt; struct:&lt;/p&gt;













 

 

 

 

 

 

 




 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 



&lt;div class="warning"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Warning:&lt;/strong&gt; Code reference &lt;code&gt;settings/structs&lt;/code&gt; not found in source files.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;A struct definition has:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt; keyword&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The struct name (&lt;code&gt;Settings&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;struct&lt;/code&gt; keyword&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A list of fields in curly braces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each field has:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A name (&lt;code&gt;AdvanceKey&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;PerfectMode&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;PracticeMode&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A type (&lt;code&gt;AdvanceKey&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;bool&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;PracticeMode&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optional struct tags (those backtick strings - we&amp;rsquo;ll cover these in the next page)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="creating-struct-instances"&gt;Creating Struct Instances&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are several ways to create a struct:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>JSON Tags and Serialization</title><link>/docs/go-tutorial/02-settings/json-tags/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/go-tutorial/02-settings/json-tags/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="json-tags-and-serialization"&gt;JSON Tags and Serialization&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Go makes it easy to convert structs to and from JSON. This is how Baboon saves settings to disk and loads them back.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="what-are-struct-tags"&gt;What Are Struct Tags?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Look at the &lt;code&gt;Settings&lt;/code&gt; struct again:&lt;/p&gt;













 

 

 

 

 

 

 




 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 



&lt;div class="warning"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Warning:&lt;/strong&gt; Code reference &lt;code&gt;settings/structs&lt;/code&gt; not found in source files.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Those strings in backticks (&lt;code&gt;`json:&amp;quot;advance_key&amp;quot;`&lt;/code&gt;) are &lt;strong&gt;struct tags&lt;/strong&gt;. They&amp;rsquo;re metadata attached to fields that other code can read.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;encoding/json&lt;/code&gt; package reads these tags to know:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Your First Session</title><link>/docs/getting-started/first-session/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/getting-started/first-session/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s walk through your first complete typing session with Baboon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="starting-the-app"&gt;Starting the App&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Launch Baboon from your terminal:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;baboon
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;You&amp;rsquo;ll see the typing screen with a word displayed in large block letters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="the-typing-phase"&gt;The Typing Phase&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id="understanding-the-display"&gt;Understanding the Display&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Header&lt;/strong&gt;: Shows &amp;ldquo;BABOON - Typing Practice&amp;rdquo; and word progress (e.g., &amp;ldquo;Word 1/30&amp;rdquo;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Main Area&lt;/strong&gt;: The current word in large block letters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Footer&lt;/strong&gt;: WPM bar and keyboard hints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="typing-your-first-word"&gt;Typing Your First Word&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Look at the word displayed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Type each letter - watch them turn green as you go&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you make a mistake, the letter turns red&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use &lt;span class="keyboard-key "&gt;Backspace&lt;/span&gt;
 to correct errors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When done, press &lt;span class="keyboard-key "&gt;Space&lt;/span&gt;
 to advance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h3 id="visual-feedback"&gt;Visual Feedback&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Letters change colour as you type:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>File I/O</title><link>/docs/go-tutorial/02-settings/file-io/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/go-tutorial/02-settings/file-io/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="file-io"&gt;File I/O&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reading and writing files is essential for any application that needs to persist data. In this page, you&amp;rsquo;ll learn how Baboon saves and loads settings files.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="the-os-package"&gt;The os Package&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Go&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;os&lt;/code&gt; package provides functions for interacting with the operating system, including file operations:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-go" data-lang="go"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;package&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; (
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;os&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;() {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;// Get the current working directory&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;dir&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;Getwd&lt;/span&gt;()
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;nil&lt;/span&gt; {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;fmt&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;Println&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Error:&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;fmt&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;Println&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Working directory:&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;dir&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;// Get the user&amp;#39;s home directory&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;home&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;UserHomeDir&lt;/span&gt;()
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;nil&lt;/span&gt; {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;fmt&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;Println&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Error:&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;fmt&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;Println&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Home directory:&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;home&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="building-file-paths"&gt;Building File Paths&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;path/filepath&lt;/code&gt; package provides cross-platform path manipulation:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>